---
/* "Ask your own ChatGPT."
 *
 * Deliberately NOT sold as "we have AI". The differentiator is the opposite:
 * we did not build a chatbot, because the owner already has one open. What they
 * lack is a way to point it at their cafe.
 *
 * The transcript is a real exchange against the anchor cafe's data — the
 * unallocated-spend finding is the same sentence the detector produces and the
 * same one in the morning brief above.
 */
import SectionShell from '../SectionShell.astro';
import MockFrame from '../mockups/MockFrame.astro';
---

<SectionShell
  id="connector"
  eyebrow="Your assistant, your cafe"
  heading="We didn't build a chatbot. You already have one."
  accent="You already have one."
  lede="Paste one link into ChatGPT or Claude and it can read your cafe — today's takings, what's selling, what your margins really are. Read-only, one permission at a time, and you can cut it off in a click."
>
  <div class="cn-grid">
    <MockFrame
      label="ChatGPT — Sahan Cafe"
      ariaLabel="A conversation with an AI assistant connected to the cafe, answering a question about untagged spending"
    >
      <div class="cn-chat">
        <p class="cn-you">How are my margins looking this month?</p>
        <div class="cn-them">
          <p>
            Your category margins currently read between <span class="num">63%</span> and
            <span class="num">75%</span> — but I'd treat those as optimistic. GoServe reports your
            books as <span class="num">63%</span> complete, and the reason is this:
          </p>
          <p class="cn-quote">
            “None of the last 30 days' Rs 91,570.00 of spending is attributed to a part of the menu,
            so profit by category counts ingredient cost only and reads high for every category.”
          </p>
          <p>
            Until that spending is tagged, every category is being credited with profit it hasn't
            earned. Want me to mark that as something you'll deal with this week?
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </MockFrame>

    <div class="cn-points">
      <div class="cn-point">
        <h3>Read-only, unless you say otherwise</h3>
        <p>
          It can read what you granted and nothing else. Your cash position stays off limits unless
          you deliberately turn it on.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cn-point">
        <h3>It cannot move your money</h3>
        <p>
          There is exactly one thing an assistant may change: marking a finding as something you'll
          deal with. It cannot take a payment, edit a price, or touch an order.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cn-point">
        <h3>Off by default, revoked in a click</h3>
        <p>
          No connection exists until you make one. Revoking stops it on the very next request, and
          you can see when each was last used.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</SectionShell>

<style>
  .cn-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 0.85fr;
    gap: clamp(28px, 4vw, 56px);
    align-items: center;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .cn-chat {
    padding: clamp(16px, 2.2vw, 24px);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .cn-you {
    align-self: flex-end;
    max-width: 80%;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    border-radius: 14px 14px 4px 14px;
    background: var(--ink-700);
    color: var(--ink-100);
  }
  .cn-them {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    color: var(--ink-200);
  }
  .cn-them p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cn-quote {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--amber-fg);
    padding-left: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-300);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .cn-points {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .cn-point h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .cn-point p {
    color: var(--ink-200);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .cn-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
